      en: "Baneh is a city in Kurdistan Province, western Iran, near the Iraqi border. At 1600 m elevation, it is a major trading center for the Kurdish population, famous for its bazaars, especially the Baneh Bazaar. The city is also known for carpet production. Economy relies on trade, agriculture, and livestock. Population is about 100,000 (2016). Baneh has a continental climate with cold winters.",
